<title>POLAND: SOCCER-ENGLAND BEAT POLAND 2-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ENGLAND BEAT POLAND 2-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>CHORZOW, Poland 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>England beat Poland 2-0</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in their World Cup European group two qualifier</p>
<p>on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Alan Shearer 5, Teddy Sheringham 90</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Poland - 1-Andrzej Wozniak; 2-Radoslaw Kaluzny, 3-Jacek</p>
<p>Zielinski, 4-Marek Jozwiak, 5-Tomasz Waldoch, 7-Krzysztof</p>
<p>Bukalski (15-Piotr Swierczewski 46), 10-Piotr Nowak (18-Cezary</p>
<p>Kucharski 68), 6-Slawimir Majak, 8-Adam Ledworn, 9-Andrzej</p>
<p>Juskowiak (16-Waldemar Adamczyk 52), 11-Jacek Dembinski</p>
<p>England - 1-David Seaman; 2-Gary Neville, 3-Sol Campbell,</p>
<p>5-Gareth Southgate, 4-Paul Ince, 6-Graeme Le Saux, 7-David</p>
<p>Beckham (15-Phil Neville 88), Paul Gascoigne (16-David Batty</p>
<p>17), 9-Alan Shearer, 10-Teddy Sheringham, 11-Robert Lee</p>
<p>Referee: Urs Meier (Switzerland)</p>
<p>    Standings	 P   W   D   L   F  A  Pts</p>
<p> Italy		  6   5   1   0  11   1  16</p>
<p> England		6   5   0   1  11   2  15</p>
<p> Poland		 5   1   1   3   3   8   4</p>
<p> Georgia		3   0   0   3   0   5   0</p>
<p> Moldova		4   0   0   4   2  11   0</p>
<p>Next match: June 7 - Georgia v Moldova</p>
</text>
